  "question": {
    "text": "The magnetic field induction at the centre of a current-carrying circular coil (coil 1) and a closed coil (coil 2), shaped as a quarter of a disc is found to be equal in magnitude. If both the coils have equal area, then find the ratio of the currents flowing in coil 2 and coil 1.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> be the radius of circular and quarter circular coil, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>&#960;x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;I</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">'</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">'</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>",
